{"id": "EUVD-2026-32367", "enisaUuid": "80604681-f31d-3cad-bb6c-0fe4c5b61364", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfilter: nf_tables: revert commit_mutex usage in reset path\n\nIt causes circular lock dependency between commit_mutex, nfnl_subsys_ipset\nand nlk_cb_mutex when nft reset, ipset list, and iptables-nft with '-m set'\nrule run at the same time.\n\nPrevious patches made it safe to run individual reset handlers concurrently\nso commit_mutex is no longer required to prevent this.", "datePublished": "2026-05-27T12:17:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:40:57", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b0dd8637fbaae8405eb9e8de741f9ce7c9667b6f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d66bedfe97a2bc321fa8118e669aae988038f729", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f6410d18c1e2da325df02be989d5bca5ed38b086", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ee3978b6a0dcd4215cb7cedcba705a12174786a7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7f261bb906bf527c4a6e2a646e2d5f3679f2a8bc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-45901", "GHSA-jhvq-4r2h-7c2q"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01013d8a-b410-3594-921e-1c7041d7658b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "1483c6b2-544d-3ae1-9098-f01e6263fcec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3cb03edb4de33fd04c4ea55f47397b96a8657c53 <ee3978b6a0dcd4215cb7cedcba705a12174786a7"}, {"id": "18f05f34-c691-3471-9516-e4ba4c393e02", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.48 <6.6.160"}, {"id": "1a50a9b1-9fd3-3b80-afe0-1164c68d2944", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1.107 <6.2"}, {"id": "22dd9476-cfb0-3a6c-8eb7-4ad82d0bfb42", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "234b011b-efff-3a0e-b9a1-72f0fb8ac0a2", "product": {"name": "Lin